WEBVTT

00:31:56.210 --> 00:32:02.586
SK: I would generally wake up
at around 6:15,

00:32:02.610 --> 00:32:07.026
have breakfast, work for a few hours,
take time for lunch,

00:32:07.050 --> 00:32:09.426
schedule time for exercise,

00:32:09.450 --> 00:32:12.027
schedule time to connect with people.

00:32:13.670 --> 00:32:16.816
AG: It sounds a lot like what
many of us are experiencing now.

00:32:16.840 --> 00:32:18.433
Time becomes meaningless.

00:32:19.360 --> 00:32:21.781
You've probably already heard
the most popular tips

00:32:21.805 --> 00:32:22.960
for coping with that:

00:32:22.984 --> 00:32:24.186
"Make a daily schedule."

00:32:24.210 --> 00:32:26.876
"Wear different clothes
for different parts of the day."

00:32:26.900 --> 00:32:29.376
"Have Zoom calls with family and friends."

00:32:29.400 --> 00:32:32.115
But one of the lesser-known ways
to give this time meaning